WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Campaign Optimization can help you adjust your sponsored products campaigns for better performance.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:11.371
After watching this video, you'll be able to, Optimize Targeting Strategies, Adjust Bids for Better

00:00:11.371 --> 00:00:16.500
Performance, Manage Advertising Budgets Effectively, and Use Performance Results to Improve Campaigns.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.571
First, Examine your targeting strategy.

00:00:18.571 --> 00:00:22.300
In Seller Central, Select Advertising, then the Campaign Manager.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:28.100
Access Sponsored Ads, Reports Under Measurement, and Reporting to Access the Search Term Report.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.965
Review these reports weekly to identify high-performing keywords and categories.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:38.715
For example, discovering wooden cooking utensils, outperforms kitchen tools, allows you to refine

00:00:38.715 --> 00:00:39.600
your targeting.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.711
Best practices include building manual campaigns based on automatic campaign insights, creating

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:50.674
negative targeting lists for underperforming terms, and using multiple targeting types for a balanced

00:00:50.674 --> 00:00:51.100
approach.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.408
Next, let's explore bidding strategies.

00:00:53.408 --> 00:00:58.023
Dynamic bids are Amazon's automated adjustments based on conversion likelihood.

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:03.100
Dynamic bids down only lowers bids when conversion is less likely.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.580
Dynamic bids up and down, adjust bids up or down based on conversion likelihood.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.100
Allow at least two to three weeks before making bid adjustments.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:17.009
Best practices include analyzing conversion rates across placements, increasing bids for high-converting

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:21.100
placements, and regularly monitoring and updating for optimal performance.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.300
Consider increasing bids for top-of-search placements.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.300
Finally, let's optimize budget management.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.100
In the Campaign Manager, access the Budget Report in Sponsored Ads, Reports.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.700
Check these reports to monitor time and budget metrics, identify high-performing campaigns needing

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.100
more budget, and set up automated rules based on performance goals.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.671
Consider increasing budget for top-performing campaigns while reducing spend on lower-performing

00:01:46.671 --> 00:01:47.100
ones.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:53.464
Common optimization mistakes to avoid, making too many changes at once, not allowing sufficient

00:01:53.464 --> 00:01:57.100
time for results, and setting unrealistic performance targets.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.814
Remember, optimization is ongoing.

00:01:58.814 --> 00:02:05.671
Consider adjusting your ads and then monitor results for two to four weeks before making further

00:02:05.671 --> 00:02:06.100
changes.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:13.600
Key metrics to monitor, click through rates, CTR, conversion rates, advertising cost of sales, ACOS,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.100
return on ad spend, ROAS, and overall sales growth.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:23.100
Start optimizing your campaigns in the advertising console.
